GSH_OpenGL_Libretro: don't treat GLEW_ERROR_NO_GLX_DISPLAY as fatal

Under Wayland the core loaded, negotiated its GL context, then rendered
nothing at all while audio kept playing, printing only:

    InitializeImpl
    Error: Unknown error

That message is glewInit() failing. glewInit() calls glewContextInit() first
-- which is what actually loads the GL entry points -- and only then probes
GLX via glxewInit(). libglew is built against GLX (its Buildroot package
depends on xlib_libX11/Xext/Xi/Xmu, with no EGL support), so on a native
Wayland session there is no GLX display current and that probe returns
GLEW_ERROR_NO_GLX_DISPLAY. The GL function pointers are perfectly valid; only
the GLX extension table is missing, which a Wayland/EGL client never uses.

InitializeImpl treated any non-GLEW_OK result as fatal and returned early,
skipping CGSH_OpenGL::InitializeImpl() and leaving the GS handler
uninitialised -- hence a blank screen with working sound.

The diagnostic was actively misleading too: GLEW 2.2.0's _glewErrorString[]
table has five entries and its last one, index 4, is the literal string
"Unknown error" -- which doubles as the clamp for out-of-range codes.
GLEW_ERROR_NO_GLX_DISPLAY *is* 4, so the one error that matters here prints
as "Unknown error" instead of mentioning GLX.

Ignore that specific code. Guarded by #ifdef since it only exists in GLEW
builds that have GLX support at all.

Reproduced on sm8250 (Adreno 650, Mesa 26.1.3, sway) with RetroArch glcore.

Signed-off-by: REG-Linux <reglinux@reglinux.org>

--- a/Source/ui_libretro/GSH_OpenGL_Libretro.cpp
+++ b/Source/ui_libretro/GSH_OpenGL_Libretro.cpp
@@ -30,6 +30,23 @@
 #if defined(USE_GLEW)
 	glewExperimental = GL_TRUE;
 	auto result = glewInit();
+#ifdef GLEW_ERROR_NO_GLX_DISPLAY
+	//Expected and harmless under Wayland. glewInit() runs glewContextInit()
+	//first -- which is what actually loads the GL entry points, and which
+	//succeeded if we got this far -- and only then probes GLX via glxewInit().
+	//libglew is built against GLX (libglew.mk depends on xlib_libX11), so with
+	//no GLX display current that probe returns GLEW_ERROR_NO_GLX_DISPLAY.
+	//
+	//Treating it as fatal skipped CGSH_OpenGL::InitializeImpl() below, leaving
+	//the GS handler uninitialised: the core rendered nothing while audio kept
+	//playing. Worse, GLEW 2.2.0's _glewErrorString[] table ends at index 4, so
+	//glewGetErrorString() reports this as the thoroughly unhelpful
+	//"Unknown error" rather than naming GLX.
+	if(result == GLEW_ERROR_NO_GLX_DISPLAY)
+	{
+		result = GLEW_OK;
+	}
+#endif
 	CLog::GetInstance().Warn(LOG_NAME, "glewInit %d\n", result == GLEW_OK);
 	assert(result == GLEW_OK);
 	if(result != GLEW_OK)
